direction.description:
On calls 2–5, where the call said the sprint took the project: Where the sprint took the project, read from what changed and what was shown:
toward — new evidence on a task, or work that plainly moves the goal;
sideways — work was done, but outside the tasks and not moving the goal;
stalled — something happened, but no task moved: no new evidence, the same tasks open;
idle — nothing at all was done; only when the input says nothing changed. Null when the call did not say; never guess.
